<title>GERMANY: Cartel office clears Thyssen buy of G&amp;L.</title>
<headline>Cartel office clears Thyssen buy of G&amp;L.</headline>
<dateline>DUESSELDORF, Germany 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany's Federal Cartel Office has cleared the planned takeover of U.S. machinebuilder Giddings &amp; Lewis by steel group Thyssen AG, Thyssen said in a brief statement on Thursday.</p>
<p>Thyssen has made a tender offer for G&amp;L via its TAQU Inc. unit which will remain open until July 30.  </p>
<p>Cartel office clears Thyssen buy of G&amp;L</p>
<p>Cartel office approval averts a potential delay that might have resulted from it calling for an in-depth review of the regulatory impact of the takeover offer.</p>
<p>Thyssen said last week that 96 percent of G&amp;L shares had been tendered to it already.</p>
</text>
